# ArkadeOS boot screen (round 8b, approved 2026-11-14). Written by
# art/boot-sprites.js from art/boot.script.in and the drawing in
# art/boot_scene.py; change those, not this file.
#
# Sparks rush in from the dark, the six crystal bezel pieces of the Start mark
# fly in and lock with a glint each, the gem ignites with a flash, a flare and
# two hexagonal shock waves, the rays shoot out and the ARKADEOS word comes up.
# Until the desktop comes a light runs round the mark's 36 ticks (the loading
# sign), a sheen sweeps the bezel, slow beams turn behind it, motes drift out.
# Every sprite was rendered from the drawing; this moves them with its timing.
# The system's own prompts (disk password, update progress) take the word's
# place under the mark.
#
# In Plymouth's script a name inside a function means the global of that name
# when one exists, so every function brings in its own helpers as local.
# (round 8: an ease() writing the global i hung the refresh loop).

Window.SetBackgroundTopColor(0, 0, 0);
Window.SetBackgroundBottomColor(0, 0, 0);

